        "description": "Cost, durability, and finish quality comparison for removing wallpaper vs painting over it in Central Florida homes.",
        "author": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC."
        },
        "publisher": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC.",
          "logo": {
            "@type": "ImageObject",
            "url": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/images/logo.png"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/wallpaper-removal-vs-paint-kissimmee/#breadcrumbs",
        "itemListElement": [
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 1,
            "name": "Home",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 2,
            "name": "Guides",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 3,
            "name": "Wallpaper Removal vs Paint",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/wallpaper-removal-vs-paint-kissimmee"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }}
>
  <Header />

  <section class="bg-gopro-charcoal text-white py-16 border-b-4 border-gopro-orange">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <nav class="text-sm mb-6 font-sans">
        <a href="/" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <a href="/guides" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Guides</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <span class="text-white">Wallpaper Removal vs Paint</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-4 tracking-tight">Wallpaper Removal vs Paint in Kissimmee</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-3xl font-sans">
        Should you remove old wallpaper or paint over it? Cost, durability & finish quality compared.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-padding">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6 font-sans">
            You've got <a href="/services/wallpaper" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">old wallpaper</a> and you want it gone. The question every <a href="/areas/kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Kissimmee</a> homeowner asks: can I just paint over it, or do I need to remove it first? The short answer: removal is almost always better, but there are a few situations where painting over wallpaper works.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <strong>Remove wallpaper if:</strong> It's peeling, bubbling, textured, or vinyl-coated. Removal gives you a clean, smooth surface that paint bonds to properly. The finish lasts longer and looks better.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <strong>Paint over wallpaper if:</strong> The wallpaper is smooth, firmly adhered, has no seams showing, and you're okay with lower durability. It's a time-saver but comes with risks.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Wallpaper Removal: The Right Way</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4 font-sans">
            Removing wallpaper is labor-intensive but gives you the best foundation for <a href="/services/interior-exterior-painting" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">painting</a>. Here's what's involved:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li>Score the wallpaper so removal solution penetrates</li>
            <li>Apply wallpaper remover (chemical or steam)</li>
            <li>Scrape off wallpaper (sometimes in layers if multiple papers were applied)</li>
            <li>Wash walls to remove adhesive residue</li>
            <li>Patch and sand any <a href="/services/drywall" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">drywall</a> damage left behind</li>
            <li>Prime walls before painting</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <strong>Cost in Kissimmee:</strong> DIY wallpaper removal takes 1-3 days for a typical room (depending on stubbornness of the paper). Professional removal $200-$600 per room depending on size and number of wallpaper layers.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <strong>Result:</strong> Smooth walls that paint bonds to properly. Finish lasts 5-7 years with no peeling or bubbling.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Painting Over Wallpaper: When It Works</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4 font-sans">
            Painting over wallpaper can work if the wallpaper meets these conditions:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Smooth, flat wallpaper</strong> (not textured, embossed, or fabric-backed)</li>
            <li><strong>Firmly adhered</strong> with no peeling, bubbling, or loose corners</li>
            <li><strong>Seams barely visible</strong> (seams will show through paint)</li>
            <li><strong>Non-vinyl surface</strong> (vinyl won't bond with paint)</li>
            <li><strong>Not glossy</strong> (glossy paper needs heavy sanding or primer)</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <strong>Process for painting over wallpaper:</strong> Test adhesion (press firmly—if wallpaper doesn't lift, it's solid). Clean the surface (grease and dust prevent bonding). Prime with oil-based or shellac primer (water-based primers can loosen wallpaper glue). Paint two coats.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <strong>Cost in Kissimmee:</strong> Same as regular painting ($300-$600 per room) but you save the $200-$600 removal cost.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">The Risks of Painting Over Wallpaper</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Seams show through:</strong> Wallpaper seams create slight ridges that are visible after painting, especially in direct light.</li>
            <li><strong>Moisture loosens adhesive:</strong> Paint primer (especially water-based) can reactivate old wallpaper glue, causing bubbling or peeling.</li>
            <li><strong>Texture shows:</strong> Any texture, embossing, or pattern in the wallpaper will show through painted finish.</li>
            <li><strong>Shorter lifespan:</strong> Paint over wallpaper often starts peeling within 2-3 years, especially in humid Kissimmee climates.</li>
            <li><strong>Makes future removal harder:</strong> Once you paint over wallpaper, removing it later is harder. The paint seals the paper and makes scraping tedious.</li>
          </ul>

          <div class="bg-gopro-orange/10 border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6 my-8">
            <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
              <strong>Our take:</strong> We recommend removal in 90% of cases. Kissimmee's humidity makes paint-over-wallpaper more likely to fail (moisture reactivates old glue). The extra cost of removal pays off in a better finish that lasts longer. If you're repainting to sell or refresh a vacation rental, removal is especially important—buyers and guests notice seams and texture.
            </p>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Wallpaper in Kissimmee Homes</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Many Kissimmee homes built in the 1980s-90s have wallpaper in kitchens, bathrooms, or bedrooms—often multiple layers that previous owners painted or papered over. Humidity from Florida's climate can make old wallpaper adhesive soften over time, causing bubbling. If your wallpaper is already showing signs of lifting, removal is the only option.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Common Questions</h2>
          
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-white border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-2 tracking-wide">Can I paint over vinyl wallpaper?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
                Not recommended. Vinyl doesn't bond with paint primers or paints. The finish will peel quickly. Remove vinyl wallpaper before painting.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-2 tracking-wide">How do I know if wallpaper is vinyl?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
                Vinyl wallpaper feels slick or plasticky. Try peeling a corner—vinyl often peels away in sheets, leaving paper backing on the wall.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-2 tracking-wide">Will wallpaper removal damage my drywall?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
                Sometimes. If wallpaper was applied without primer or directly to drywall, removal can tear the paper facing. We patch any damage, sand smooth, and prime before painting.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-2 tracking-wide">Can I use a steamer to remove wallpaper?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
                Yes. Steamers work well on old, stubborn wallpaper. The heat softens adhesive so paper scrapes off easier. Chemical removers also work but take longer to penetrate.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <strong>Remove wallpaper</strong> if you want a smooth, long-lasting paint finish. It costs more upfront but gives better results. <strong>Paint over wallpaper</strong> only if it's smooth, firmly stuck, and you're okay with visible seams and shorter lifespan. In Kissimmee's humid climate, removal is almost always the better choice.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-8 my-8">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide">Need Wallpaper Removal or Painting?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-6">
              We remove wallpaper and <a href="/services/interior-exterior-painting" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">paint</a> walls in <a href="/areas/kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Kissimmee</a>, <a href="/areas/orlando" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Orlando</a>, and Central Florida. Free estimates. Full surface prep so paint lasts.
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
              <a href="/estimate" class="btn-primary">
                Get Free Estimate
              </a>
              <a href="tel:4072446873" class="btn-secondary">
                Call (407) 244-6873
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 font-sans">
              <a href="/guides" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">← Back to All Guides</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection
    title="Ready to Remove Wallpaper & Paint?"
    description="Professional wallpaper removal and painting. Smooth finish, lasting results. Serving Kissimmee & Central Florida."
  />

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
